. "$GRIMOIRE"/CMAKE_FUNCTIONS
           SPELL=mt32emu
         VERSION=2.8.2
          SOURCE=munt-$VERSION.tar.gz
SOURCE_DIRECTORY=$BUILD_DIRECTORY/munt-$VERSION
        WEB_SITE=https://munt.sourceforge.net/
   SOURCE_URL[0]=https://downloads.sourceforge.net/project/munt/munt/$VERSION/$SOURCE
     SOURCE_HASH=sha512:cedc9ec1ae7a999dd031f8c1bcfd1128c7ea56f792990395a82535da4a046a73a667356041537f1455a7a1e043e21888efd559ccbc4f0684c97e4d83c041008f
      LICENSE[0]=GPL
         ENTERED=20260927
           SHORT="Roland MT-32 and CM-32L software synthesizer"
cat << EOF
MUNT is a software synthesizer emulating the Roland MT-32, the CM-32L and
the closely related CM-64 and LAPC-I. Only libmt32emu is packaged here; the
stand-alone emulator, the smf2wav converter and the Qt front-end are not
built.

The library installs as libmt32emu, with a pkg-config file (mt32emu) and a
CMake package (MT32Emu) exporting the MT32Emu::mt32emu target.
